      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add disableBoundaryAwareCache compat option for prefix-matching prompt cache providers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where DeepSeek OpenAI-compatible users could lose provider prompt-cache hits after the 6.x boundary-aware cache split put per-turn dynamic context into the system prompt.\n\nCloses #94518\n\nRelated: #91018, #90583\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDeepSeek uses prefix-matching cache behavior, so its stable system prefix needs to remain byte-stable across turns. This PR adds `compat.disableBoundaryAwareCache`, defaults it on for DeepSeek, keeps only the stable prefix in the system message, and moves the dynamic suffix into the latest user turn so older conversation history stays reusable.\n\nXiaomi is kept opt-in — users can set `compat.disableBoundaryAwareCache: true` manually, but the automatic default is DeepSeek-only until Xiaomi-specific upstream cache-contract and live-behavior evidence exists.\n\nOperators can opt back into normal boundary-aware behavior with `compat: { disableBoundaryAwareCache: false }`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDeepSeek users should keep the stable system prompt and prior conversation history cacheable across multi-turn requests instead of invalidating the reusable prefix with each dynamic suffix update. Xiaomi users are unaffected by default.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/ai/src/providers/openai-completions.test.ts`: 41 passed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/openai-transport-stream.test.ts`: 302 passed\n\nReal production request-shape proof (imports the actual `buildOpenAICompletionsParams` production module):\n\n```text\n$ npx tsx deepseek-proof.ts\n--- DeepSeek (disableBoundaryAwareCache: true) ---\nsystem.content=\"You are helpful\"\nsystem.hasDynamicSuffix=true\nmsg1.role=user\nmsg1.content=\"Historical request\"\nmsg2.role=assistant\nlastUser.hasDynamicSuffix=true\nlastUser.hasCurrentRequest=true\n\n--- DeepSeek (disableBoundaryAwareCache: false) ---\nsystem.content=\"You are helpful\nProject Context\"\nlastUser.hasDynamicSuffix=true\n\n--- GPT (boundary stripped, no split) ---\nsystem.content=\"You are helpful\nProject Context\"\nsystem.hasBoundary=false\nlastUser.hasDynamicSuffix=false\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>deepseek-proof.ts</summary>\n\n```ts\nimport { SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_BOUNDARY } from \"@openclaw/ai/internal/shared\";\nimport { buildOpenAICompletionsParams } from \"../../worktrees/pr-95311/src/agents/openai-transport-stream.js\";\nimport type { Model } from \"openclaw/plugin-sdk/llm\";\n\nfunction deepseekModel(): Model<\"openai-completions\"> {\n  return {\n    id: \"deepseek-v4-pro\", name: \"DeepSeek V4 Pro\",\n    api: \"openai-completions\", provider: \"deepseek\",\n    baseUrl: \"https://api.deepseek.com\",\n    compat: { thinkingFormat: \"deepseek\" },\n    reasoning: true, input: [\"text\"],\n    cost: { input: 0, output: 0, cacheRead: 0, cacheWrite: 0 },\n    contextWindow: 1_000_000, maxTokens: 384_000,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction main() {\n  const ds = buildOpenAICompletionsParams(deepseekModel(), {\n    systemPrompt: `You are helpful${SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_BOUNDARY}Project Context`,\n    messages: [\n      { role: \"user\", content: \"Historical request\", timestamp: 1 },\n      { role: \"assistant\", content: \"Historical answer\", timestamp: 2 },\n      { role: \"user\", content: \"Current request\", timestamp: 3 },\n    ],\n    tools: [],\n  } as never, undefined);\n  const msgs = (ds as any).messages;\n  console.log(\"--- DeepSeek (disableBoundaryAwareCache: true) ---\");\n  console.log(`system.content=\"${msgs[0]?.content}\"`);\n  // ... full proof in outputs/issue-94518/deepseek-proof.ts\n}\n\nmain();\n```\n\n</details>\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
